Z||000005||Coconut||09-15-2000||03:31 PM||||The weather here in WA. is still pretty nice for the most part,but it is starting to get  cold on the way to work. I hate to admit it but snowy's right, it's almost time for my pegasus to hibernate for the winter. I'm gonna have to find a few spots where I can really "open up" the ol' V6 before it's time to put her into the stable. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I figure I've got a month or two left, I'd better enjoy 'em. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||snowkttn||09-15-2000||04:46 PM||||Hey Coconut!!  Glad to see you again!<P>Where in WA are you?  Yup, gonna miss my driving my toy......  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">(((<P>Batboy?  Is that really you? hehehehe||||reg||10
Z||000007||Coconut||09-15-2000||06:27 PM||||Hey there, Snowkittn!<P>Me and FieroGTGirl are out here in Puyallup (home of the Western Washington Fair) We went to the Fair last evening and checked out the Steve Miller Band (She had gotten tickets for this since May) I really wasn't up to going at first,(short handed at work, so it was an especially exhausting day) but she talked me into it. WOW! What a really GREAT time we had! I was really impressed with their performance. Great bunch of musicians. Norton Buffalo has got to be THE BEST blues harmonica player that I have ever heard......BAR NONE!<BR>Anyway, good to hear from ya, Snowy <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Thanks for the welcome back!<P>Cruisin' On, <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||7
Z||000008||gixxer||09-15-2000||07:01 PM||||Weeeelll Coconut, use MY racetrack. From Puyallup, go down Hwy 7 to Elbe. Then South to Morton. Go East on Hwy 12 to Randle. Go south on forest road 25 (about 45 miles of twisties on the east side of Mount Saint Helens, and no cops) to Eagle Cliffs, forest road 90. Go east on FR 90 to Wind River road(much of this road is brand spanking new), which goes to Carson. Now you're on the Columbia, so find your way back.<BR>I just ran this a couple of days ago and it was excellent.<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Coconut||09-15-2000||08:38 PM||||Right On gixxer!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I've done the first part of that run as far as Randall and gotta say it is some good stuff! You've got my curiosity brewing with FR 90 Eastbound. Haven't tried that yet <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Thanks for the input. Sounds like some excellent advice. BTW~ Ya know, I drive a company freight truck every morning from Tacoma into Kent and I usually see a Fiero or 3 heading into work and I'm constantly wondering "Could that be gixxer". Whatch'a driving dude? Anyway, if ya see a big white freight truck with a Cronin Co. Logo that says "Run with the Pack" and some long haired Islander looking dude, grinning and admiring your Fiero...... well that would be me <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Cruisin' On, <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||gixxer||09-15-2000||10:53 PM||||Might not be me. I commute from Kent to Renton and back, on the backroads, usually not on 167. <BR>Have an almost stock yellow Formula with dark tinted glass and a sunroof. Probably the only one like that in the area.<BR>Be looking for ya anyway Coconut!||||reg||1
